                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Lawyer, Playwrite, Politician, Government Informer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Leonard MacNally was a Protestant Irish Republican turned British
                            government paid informer. Prior to becoming an informer for the British
                            Government in 1794, he had been a successful and loyal member of the
                            Irish Unionists movement, aiding in the defence of many being prosecuted
                            by the British government. However, after betraying the cause, he would
                            regularly relay information and court tactics back to the British,
                            hindering the movement and going undetected until after his death in
                            1820. </p>
                            
                         <p>It is possible that he knew Godwin through connections with the
                            Currans, with both parties being implicated at different times with
                            Wolfe Tone.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> </bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title/> DNB, Ed Pope </bibl>
                </person>
